<description>&lt;p&gt;The International Court of Justice ruled that Myanmar committed genocide against the Rohingya, prompting Myanmar to reject the verdict as unfair while rights groups called for sanctions. The junta has destroyed bridges in Arakan, moved west of the Sittaung River, and is planning a 108‑kilometre fence on the Bangladesh border, while an airstrike hit a displacement camp in Rakhine. In Sagaing, junta forces killed 11 people and Starlink outages isolated communities, and health-care facilities continued to be attacked in October 2026. There were 2,332 battle-related deaths in 2024, according to UCDP.&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;em&gt;Machine-written from the linked sources, checked for figures and names not in them.&lt;/em&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&quot;https://www.bbc.co.uk/news/articles/c804wzp20ddvo?at_medium=RSS&amp;amp;at_campaign=rss&quot;&gt;BBC News&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/focus/20261120-malaysia-s-unwanted-refugees-the-plight-of-the-rohingya&quot;&gt;France 24&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.theguardian.com/global-development/2026/nov/19/everyone-struggled-for-this-justice-tears-in-court-as-rohingya-vindicated-in-myanmar-genocide-ruling&quot;&gt;The Guardian&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Washington Post&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.com/rss/articles/CBMiwAFBVV95cUxNZk1JdVF0VUhUY0NYWEpCREVXNEJkRnE3M2JmcmpNeVhVMm0xejVJeWl5SDlPNzZlLWF1cUVlblgxMERydzd5emY2OHc2anY1Wk9acFV6Tk1uTUNlZFkxNHZJTjdnUTQwN2l5U19nRzdfUTZBMUNTMWNIVVJjOTllSHA0TWpDYnk2U3Y2VFlaSzVHTlNGMGFFUThfUnh2YjhLU2xqeUhLM2Zuc1hPMnZZUnlTeHpISWN1SHNSNGNjaUY?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Washington Post&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.aljazeera.com/news/2026/11/20/what-does-the-icjs-rohingya-genocide-ruling-mean-for-gaza?traffic_source=rss&quot;&gt;Al Jazeera&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://news.google.?oc=5&quot;&gt;The Washington Post&lt;/a&gt;, &lt;a href=&quot;https://www.theguardi